Excavation Log – Site

We found something today. Not a bone, not a tool. A mark.

Carved into the underside of a stone slab, about two meters down. The site supervisor almost missed it. Said it looked like a scratch.

I had it photographed and enlarged. It's not random.

The layer dates to roughly 1200 BCE. No known writing system from that period matches these characters.

But here's the strange part.

I showed the photo to one of the local assistants. He looked at it for a few seconds and said, "Oh, I've seen that before."

I asked where.

He said, “I don't know.”
